 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Resolves an [RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901) against a JSON document.
+The empty string selects the entire document. Other pointers begin with `/`; `/` separated tokens
+select object members or array elements. Within a token, `~1` represents `/` and `~0` represents `~`.
+Array indices use `0` or a non-zero digit followed by digits, with no leading zeroes. The function
+returns the selected value (including `null`) and throws if the pointer is malformed or does not
+resolve within the document.
